# Pin line endings for files that bash / sh / node must execute. Without this,
# a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for Windows default) re-converts
# these to CRLF on checkout, and the bundled scripts then fail on macOS / Linux
# with `$'\r': command not found` (see issue #1).
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# JavaScript helpers we ship in resources/claude-integration/ — also stay LF so
# Node on macOS / Linux doesn't have to deal with stray CR characters.
*.js    text eol=lf

# Markdown command definitions — Claude Code reads these; LF is the safe default.
*.md    text eol=lf

# Source code stays text but lets Git use the platform default — Kotlin / Gradle
# tooling handles either.
*.kt    text
*.java  text
*.xml   text
*.json  text
